ut, so it's easy to find different varietals of wine. They also sell a small selection of cheeses and meats, as well as beer and liquor. It's also dog friendly, so bring your furry friends! The owner actually ha a bag of treats for our well behaved four legged friends. I highly recommend checking this place out for your next dinner party or other wine needs. Defi..."},{"business_id":"dDXDmROCvIEYxvQYWXsKpQ","review_id":"6nbTO6L9eOLjotwtv8Wlxg","date":"2017-04-15T02:44:48","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9348642826080322,"text_excerpt":"Stopped in to do a little Easter Brunch prepping and found the shop to be really quaint. The wine and spirit selection is small but well curated. From my quick perusing I saw wines from all over the world. Was extremely impressed with their Scotch offerings as well as their Mezcales. If you're looking for a great gift for a wine aficionado or a Scotch/Whiskey lover this is your spot."},{"business_id":"dDXDmROCvIEYxvQYWXsKpQ","review_id":"s0lN4mX4dOUggwYWWSYceg","date":"2021-07-31T21:28:55","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.930892288684845,"text_excerpt":"Love this place. They do free tastings every Friday from 5-7 (usually 4-5 wines in the $15-40 range). They also have a great selection of wines in the $20-30 range and a bunch of super fun/funky natural wines. The owner is really knowledgeable and will happily recommend wines you'll like in your price range."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
